;; The read level's divergences from gcc 15.2 on the C23 corpus (doc/C23-SURVEY.md, "As built: C7 (write-ahead)"; bin/ci
;; dg): the classes every file of the dg check (the checker's errors against the dg-error lines, by line and kind) that
;; does not pass falls into, in test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A file's class is the first whose :match finds its
;; result and reason ("RESULT REASON", as test/c/check-dg-linux-amd64.edn writes them: "missed: missed [LINES] expecting:
;; MESSAGE" an expected error line without an error of the checker's, "extra: extra [LINES] got: ERROR" an error on a line
;; that expects none, "both:" both, "refused:", "timeout:", "crash:" the read gave no judgment). The first four are the
;; checker's and the preprocessor's diagnostics C4 and C2 did not widen (CS92 (a), CS94 (a): left to C7's judge, which
;; records them); the last are reader gaps. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :attr-diag
  :title "attribute misuse the checker does not diagnose"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "gcc diagnoses a standard attribute given arguments it does not take, in a place it does not apply to, or ignored; the checker keeps attributes as data (C4.4's list, CS92 (a))"
  :decided "CS92 (a)"
  :match [#"expecting: (.*ignored|.*does not take any arguments|parentheses must be omitted|.*invalid use of attribute|.*'fallthrough' attribute|.*attribute 'fallthrough'|only weak|.*invalid vector type|attributes before C23|requires an identifier|impossible constraint|.*attribute.*not preceding)"]}
 {:id :decl-diag
  :title "declaration, type and constant-expression errors the checker does not give"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "conflicting and redefined tags and types (C23's tag compatibility), incompatible pointers, constexpr and enumeration range checks, VLA and empty-initializer rules, static assertion, bit-fields: C4.4 diagnosed the errors cc's checker and the corpora needed; the rest is the long tail of gcc's c-typeck and c-decl"
  :decided "CS92 (a)"
  :match [#"expecting: (conflicting|redefinition|redeclaration|incompatible|incomplete|nested|jump|bit-field|storage class|declared with but defined|declared both|'enum' declared|old-style|too many arguments|pointer type mismatch|return discards|ordered comparison|not an integer constant|use of type name|file-scope compound|static but declared|'bool'|cannot use keyword|zero or negative|array of unknown size|variable-sized|declared in underspecified|duplicate case|static assertion|from a string literal|.*outside the range|overflow in enumeration|invalid 'enum'|.*constexpr|.*empty declaration|'signed _BitInt'|'_BitInt'|assignment to|passing argument|applied to a bit-field|expected (expression before|'\S{1,6}'$)|empty declaration|storage class specifier|'enum' underlying|used but never defined)"]}
 {:id :pedantic-diag
  :title "pedwarns of -pedantic-errors the checker does not know"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "gcc turns its pedantic warnings into errors under -pedantic-errors, which most of these tests give; the checker's pedantic mode (CS132 (a), the file's -pedantic-errors) has the C23 corpus's imaginary constants, case ranges, named loops, 0o, wb and string concatenation, and the rest of the pedwarns are not diagnosed (digit separators, complex ++, delimited escapes, __VA_OPT__ before C2y, #embed before C23 in a plain directive), and one the checker gives that gcc does not: #embed's pedwarn inside __extension__ (embed-2; review 006, finding 3 narrowed parse-gap's catch-all that held it)"
  :decided "CS92 (a)"
  :match [#"expecting: (imaginary constants|ISO C does not|.*does not support|.*not supported|implicit|non-standard concatenation|'0o' prefixed|digit separator|.*before C23|delimited escape|'__VA_OPT__' is not available|.*traditional)" #"^fail extra: extra \[[\d ]+\] got: \d+: '#embed' before C23 is a GCC extension"]}
 {:id :pp-diag
  :title "preprocessor diagnostics the port does not give"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the port's errors with no position (\"-: ...\": an extra __has_c_attribute operand error, #embed's expected '('; review 006, finding 1), #embed parameters given twice or malformed, universal character names that are invalid or not in NFC, __VA_OPT__ misuse, pasting that makes no token, #elifdef nesting: the port's preprocessor diagnoses what cc's did (C2.4's list, CS50-CS51)"
  :decided "CS50, CS51"
  :match [#"expecting: (duplicate embed|expected parameter|operator '|division by zero|unknown embed|negative embed|too large|'defined' in|expected character string|expected '|'gnu::base64'|.*valid universal character|.*not valid in an identifier|.*not in NFC|unterminated '__VA_OPT__'|pasting|-:began|.*__has_embed)" #"^fail stopped: \d+ errors? not located in the main file: -: (operator \"__has_c_attribute\" requires|expected '\(')"]}
 {:id :parse-gap
  :title "valid C23 (or an error test's other lines) the parser rejects"
  :kind :gap
  :why "the parser stops at a construct of C23 or of gcc's testsuite that repr/c does not read yet (C2Y's if declarations are read since CS194 (a); an #embed whose directory is ${srcdir}'s is found since CS192 (a); the read's error where embed-10's checker error is expected (review 006, finding 7); attribute positions, compound literals with storage classes, _Generic with a type argument, va_start without a parameter, named loops, labels before declarations, tag redefinitions in members); the file's later expected lines are then missed"
  :decided "C7"
  :match [#"^fail missed: missed \[5\] \(read errors \[5\], the checker not run\) expecting: makes pointer from integer without a cast"
          #"^fail extra: .* got: [^ ]*:\d+:\d+: unexpected" #"^fail extra: .* got: [^ ]*:\d+:\d+: (strconv|\"|#)"]}
 {:id :read-refused
  :title "the reader or converter refuses, times out or crashes"
  :kind :gap
  :why "a declarator the converter reads as not a function's, decimal floating suffixes (by design, CS3 (a)), integer suffixes beyond 128 bits, an empty character constant; since review 006 (finding 3) only these refusals, a timeout or a crash in no class"
  :decided "C7"
  :match [#"^fail refused: convert: (floating suffix d(32|64|128|64x)|a function definition whose declarator is not a function's|invalid suffix on integer constant|empty character constant)"]}
]
